steps.body:
In a graph with `n` nodes, start with `n` groups, one per node. Every edge whose `unite` succeeds joins two groups, so the count drops by one. When the edges run out, the count left is the number of connected components, with no DFS or BFS:

```cpp harness
struct UnionFind { std::vector<int> parent; std::vector<int> size; explicit UnionFind(int n) : parent(n), size(n, 1) { std::iota(parent.begin(), parent.end(), 0); } int findRoot(int x) { if (parent[x] != x) parent[x] = findRoot(parent[x]); return parent[x]; } bool unite(int a, int b) { int ra = findRoot(a), rb = findRoot(b); if (ra == rb) return false; if (size[ra] < size[rb]) std::swap(ra, rb); parent[rb] = ra; size[ra] += size[rb]; return true; } };
{{code}}
```

```cpp
int n = 5;
std::vector<std::pair<int, int>> edges = {{0, 1}, {1, 2}, {3, 4}};
UnionFind uf(n);
int components = n;
for (const auto& [a, b] : edges) {
    if (uf.unite(a, b)) {
        --components;
    }
}
std::cout << components << '\n';   // 2, {0 1 2} and {3 4}
```

A failed `unite` says more. It means `a` and `b` were already connected some other way, so in an undirected graph this edge closes a cycle. A connected graph on `n` nodes needs only `n - 1` edges, and the edges that fail are the extras: remove all of them and every group stays connected. Union find also handles edges as they arrive, one at a time, where a DFS would have to start over after each new edge.

example.code:
#include <iostream>
#include <numeric>
#include <utility>
#include <vector>

struct UnionFind {
    std::vector<int> parent;
    std::vector<int> size;

    explicit UnionFind(int n) : parent(n), size(n, 1) {
        std::iota(parent.begin(), parent.end(), 0);
    }

    int findRoot(int x) {
        if (parent[x] != x) {
            parent[x] = findRoot(parent[x]);
        }
        return parent[x];
    }

    bool unite(int a, int b) {
        int ra = findRoot(a);
        int rb = findRoot(b);
        if (ra == rb) {
            return false;
        }
        if (size[ra] < size[rb]) {
            std::swap(ra, rb);
        }
        parent[rb] = ra;
        size[ra] += size[rb];
        return true;
    }
};

int main() {
    int n = 0;
    int m = 0;
    std::cin >> n >> m;
    UnionFind uf(n);
    int components = n;
    for (int i = 0; i < m; ++i) {
        int a = 0;
        int b = 0;
        std::cin >> a >> b;
        if (uf.unite(a, b)) {
            --components;
        } else {
            std::cout << a << ' ' << b << " closes a cycle" << '\n';
        }
    }
    std::cout << "components " << components << '\n';
    return 0;
}

